    "factsheet": [
        {
            "heading": "Exhibition: Behind that Door",
            "paragraphs": [
                "A special exhibition exploring the rich heritage of the Wimbledon Village Club and Lecture Hall. Over the years the building has witnessed a full spectrum of experiences, providing piety and sobriety, shelter and camaraderie, conviviality and revelry. Visitors will discover the building’s links to Wimbledon’s history and the colourful characters who have crossed its threshold."
            ]
        },
        {
            "heading": "YWA Young Artists in Residence",
            "paragraphs": [
                "The winner of our YWA Young Artists in Residence competition, Alex Yam, together with our Museum Creative, Louise Hung, will be exhibiting in our Gallery"
            ]
        },
        {
            "heading": "Family Activity",
            "paragraphs": [
                "My Home – Family Drop-in Craft \nSaturday 12th September \n11 am to 4 pm\nMake a little picture of your home!",
                "What makes your home special? Is it the people, a favourite room, your garden, a pet, or something you love doing there?\nChildren can create a fold-out paper house and fill it with drawings, patterns and tiny details that show what “home” means to them."
            ]
        },
        {
            "heading": "Family Activity",
            "paragraphs": [
                "The Peacock Palace - Family story telling \nSunday 13th September\n11 am \n1 pm\nA very grand, sparkly Peacock is visiting Wimbledon Common! But where will he stay? Join @Storytime Friends (Magda and Maggie) at the Wimbledon Museum for a magical, interactive Open House weekend adventure created especially for under 5s. Packed with live music, sensory play, and friendly animal puppets, your little ones will help the woodland creatures compete to build the ultimate home. May the best house win!"
            ]
        },
        {
            "heading": "Museum Activity",
            "paragraphs": [
                "Museum Activity - What makes Wimbledon, Wimbledon?  Saturday 12th and Sunday 13th September 11 am to 4 pm",
                "What do you think of Wimbledon?",
                "Historic? Charming? Crowded? Green? Lively?\nWhat’s your word for Wimbledon?\nAdd your opinion to other people’s and see what our community thinks."
            ]
        }
    ],
